#!/bin/bash
# demiurge-run-cpp <binary-or-source>
# If given an executable, runs it directly. If given a .cpp source
# that has no matching binary, compiles it once with the DEMIURGE
# default flags, then runs the result.
set -e
source /opt/demiurge/lib/demiurge-env.sh 2>/dev/null || source "$(dirname "$0")/../lib/demiurge-env.sh"

if [[ -z "$1" ]]; then
    echo "usage: demiurge-run-cpp <binary-or-source.cpp>" >&2
    exit 1
fi

TARGET="$1"; shift

# If target is source, one-shot compile next to it
if [[ "$TARGET" == *.cpp && ! -x "$TARGET" ]]; then
    OUT="${TARGET%.cpp}"
    echo "demiurge-run-cpp: building $TARGET → $OUT" >&2
    g++ -O2 -o "$OUT" "$TARGET" -ljack -lasound -lm -lpthread
    TARGET="$OUT"
fi

# If target exists without extension but source sits next to it, same idea
if [[ ! -x "$TARGET" && -f "${TARGET}.cpp" ]]; then
    echo "demiurge-run-cpp: building ${TARGET}.cpp → $TARGET" >&2
    g++ -O2 -o "$TARGET" "${TARGET}.cpp" -ljack -lasound -lm -lpthread
fi

if [[ ! -x "$TARGET" ]]; then
    echo "demiurge-run-cpp: no executable at $TARGET" >&2
    exit 2
fi

exec "$TARGET" "$@"
